# The @lvlup-sw scope resolves from GitHub Packages, not npmjs.org.
#
# `@lvlup-sw/strategos-contracts` is the Zod/TypeScript projection of the
# Strategos wire contract, emitted from the same TypeSpec sources that produce
# the JSON Schema and the C# records. It is published `access: restricted` to
# the org, so a resolving client must authenticate.
#
# GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN, and deliberately NOT the conventional NODE_AUTH_TOKEN:
# `actions/setup-node` writes `//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}`
# whenever a job passes `registry-url`, which release.yml does. Sharing the name
# would send a GitHub token to npmjs.org and take a 401 on an unrelated install.
# A distinct name keeps the two registries' credentials from ever crossing.
#
#   CI    — the job's GITHUB_TOKEN, which needs `packages: read`.
#   Local — a token carrying `read:packages` (`gh auth refresh -s read:packages`).
#
# npm expands the variable at read time; an unset value yields a 401 rather than
# a silent fall-through to the public registry.
#
# This scope line does NOT redirect our own publish. `@lvlup-sw/exarchos` goes to
# npmjs.org through OIDC trusted publishing, pinned by `publishConfig.registry`
# in package.json, which outranks a scope registry.
@lvlup-sw:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN}
